      "title": "Study: what Python planners write",
      "changed": "Five models wrote plans for the 16 banking tasks, without and with the plan language stated in the prompt. Nothing executed.",
      "question": "How much of what planners write does the plan language accept, and what must it add?",
      "result": "Stating the language is the main lever (Haiku 0% → 88%, GPT-5 mini 0% → 62%). DeepSeek V3.2 ignores most rules (19%). String methods, number formats and `is None` survive the rules for every model.",
      "decision": "Add those constructs in PR 1; the planner prompt states the rules; per-model output budgets (a first run with 2000 tokens, $0.18 of the cost, was discarded: hidden reasoning cut 15 of 160 replies).",
